## Impact Analysis (Your Competitive Advantage)

Unlike text-based code search, you can answer questions that grep CANNOT.
Use this to create **better plans and tasks** that coding agents (Claude Code, Cursor, etc.) will execute.

**Before Planning Code Changes - ALWAYS Query Impact First:**
1. "Find all callers of [function/method]" - Know the blast radius
2. "What depends on [class/module]?" - Understand downstream effects
3. "What would break if I change [interface]?" - Risk assessment

**Impact Analysis Queries (use with query_graph):**
- "Find all methods that call process_payment" → Exact callers, no false positives
- "What classes inherit from BaseHandler and override handle()?" → Change propagation
- "Show the call chain from main() to database_connect()" → Dependency path
- "Find all entry points that eventually call [function]" → Trace from API to internals
- "What tests cover [class/method]?" → Test impact of changes

**When Creating Plans/Tasks for Code Changes:**
1. FIRST: Query the graph to understand what calls the code being changed
2. SECOND: Identify the blast radius (all affected components)
3. THIRD: Map which tests need to run/be updated
4. THEN: Create your plan/tasks with full awareness of impact

**Key Advantage Over Text Search:**
- Grep finds "process_payment" in comments, strings, and unrelated code
- Graph queries find ONLY actual callers via CALLS relationships
- You can traverse multiple hops: "what calls the callers of X?"
- Your plans will be more accurate because you understand the full dependency graph
